  (text "about -0.6 to -0.8 V\n(ledNeg = 0.8 V)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 157.48 111.76 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d4d83494-2e3d-57d2-ac72-802dfabb5f45"))
  (text "Section 5 of the circuit notes. LED clipping in the second stage is reported [4]; the LEDs D2 and D3 in anti-parallel,\nred, about 1.5-1.8 V, are reported by a mod [2]. Their place as a shunt to VB after the gain stage is inferred.\nUX3, RX5, RX6: stage 2 as an ideal op-amp with a fixed gain of 3 (stage2G, chosen and tuned by measurement).\nRX7: series resistor feeding the clippers (chosen). DX1: a one-sided silicon clip standing in for the off-centre biased\ndiscrete stage the notes infer for the even harmonics. The DSP's knee is x/(1+|x/0.8|^6)^(1/6) (ledNeg, negKnee, chosen)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 198.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c1bdd089-d8d8-59e3-b68e-c48a22b10e28"))
